# NAPI-RS build artifacts
*.node
npm/
# napi-rs writes a .cargo/config.toml when cross-compiling, which is why any
# .cargo directory is ignored. The workspace's own /.cargo/config.toml is not
# generated: it carries LIBSQLITE3_FLAGS and must be in source control, or CI,
# `cross` and every fresh clone silently build an untrimmed SQLite.
#
# Git will not descend into an excluded directory, so re-including one file
# takes all four lines: un-ignore the root directory, re-ignore its contents,
# then carve out the one tracked file. Nested .cargo/ directories stay ignored.
.cargo/
!/.cargo/
/.cargo/*
!/.cargo/config.toml

# Coverage and runtime artifacts
lcov.info
*.profraw
server.pid
dist/
artifacts/
.env.*
!.env.example

